        "description": "Presence of characteristic skin lesions such as nodules, plaques, or diffuse infiltration",
        "category": "minor",
        "requiredForDiagnosis": false
      }
    ],
    "minimumForDiagnosis": "At least one major criterion (hypopigmented patch with sensory loss or thickened peripheral nerve) or positive acid-fast bacilli detection",
    "notes": "Diagnosis is primarily clinical supported by laboratory confirmation when available."
